I import dates from Excel files all the time for my classes. Usually this is from a dump of stock prices from Yahoo. In the excel file the dates are in one colunn and the data are in adjacent columns. I typically use the splus gui as follows:

 

#
# 1. load Excel data into Splus using the GUI.
#  Download data from class website to local disk
#  File/Import Data/From File
#  Click [Browse] and select the file econ483lab7returns.xls
#  Name the Data set lab8.df
#  Click Options tab, and uncheck box next to Strings as factors
#  Click Okay to load the data into the data.frame lab8.df

 

This gets the data into a data frame. The column with the dates are a timeDate object. The default format shows 0:00:00.000. If you widen the column you will see the full date. With monthly data, I usually change the date format using

 

> lab8.df$Date@format = "%b %Y"

 

So that dates are now represented as, for example, "Jan 2004".

