I had a similar problem and the solution is simple, but not obvious. The default import is for the information to be a character type. You can then either convert the column to a TimeDate type, or use the ascharacter command when you want to calculate time ... here is an example from some code I wrote up: 

dosing.df$date <- timeDate(dosing.df$date,in.format="%d-%m-%Y",format="%02m/%02d/%04Y") 

Look up the timeDate command for more information on the formatting. 

Good luck, 

Nathan 
