Dates come across as a date format followed by a time format.  If all
you have is dates with no times, the times are all zeros.  Widen the
field with your dates.  You are likely to find the dates in front of all
of your zeros.

 

Then, to see the dates without all of the time zeros, right click on the
header of the column and select 'Properties'.  This will bring up the
Properties box.  On the right side select the DATE format that you like,
and set the TIME format to [None].  This will get rid of the Time zeros,
and you'll see only the Date.

*****************************************************************************

Deborah Carlson
