I've been running conditional logistic regression in SAS using PROC PHREG 
and in S using coxph().  In S, one has to specify ** method="exact" **, 
whereas in SAS one uses the ties=DISCRETE option.

The SAS ties=DISCRETE option corresponds to a discrete logistic model, 
which differs from what you get with the ties=EXACT option.  In S, there 
doesn't seem to be an option (or method) corresponding to the discrete 
logistic model.  The documentation for coxph() doesn't detail what the 
(partial?) likelihood is corresponding to the method="exact" option, so I'm 
just assuming it is the same one SAS uses (for ties=EXACT; cf. Kalbfleisch 
& Prentice, 2002, p. 104-106).

Does anyone know of a reference with more detail on the likelihoods 
underlying the coxph() estimation?  I've searched the archives, but I 
haven't found this information anywhere.

I'm running SPlus 6.2 with Windows XP.

