I'd like to name numerous objects based on an argument in a function.  An example of how I'd do it in SAS is given below .

%MACRO UPDATE(OLDMONTH,NEWMONTH);

program1&NEWMONTH = some modification of program1&OLDMONTH;

program2&NEWMONTH = some modification of program2&OLDMONTH;

program3&NEWMONTH = some modification of program3&OLDMONTH;

and so on

%MEND;

%UPDATE(Nov04,Dec04);

What I'd like to do in S-Plus is something similar where I can name the object based on the function argument.  Is there an S-Plus routine something like the following?

UPDATE <- function(OLDMONTH,NEWMONTH,...)

{

program1&NEWMONTH <- some modification of program1&OLDMONTH

program2&NEWMONTH <- some modification of program2&OLDMONTH

program3&NEWMONTH <- some modification of program3&OLDMONTH

and so on

}

Of course I could do it with individual function arguments such as 

UPDATE <- function(program1.OLDMONTH,program1.NEWMONTH,program2.OLDMONTH,program2.NEWMONTH,program3.OLDMONTH,program3.NEWMONTH,...)

But I have dozens of programs and this would become tedious and open the door for error.

Might anyone have suggestions?

Thanks in advance,

