Subject: extracting components from t.test
Message-ID: <41E2749F.4050406@nt.ntnu.no>

Dear S+ users,

I would like to (among other things) extract the t statistic from 
several t.tests. The t-statistic has the names attribute "t", but I just 
want the numbers and store them in a column.

I started by 'training' on a dummy test: t20<-t.test(rnorm(20, 1.8, 1), 
rnorm(20, 1.5, 1)).

So far I have tried different ways to extract 'statistic' and/or remove 
the names attribute "t" from one t.test output:

1. t20$statistic
2. t20["statistic"]
3. as.vector(t20[1])
...et c. which all keeps the attribute "t".

I also tried to bind the result of several dummy-t.test (t20, t30...) 
together...

stat<-rbind(t20,t30,t40,t50)
...and then extract components
stat$statistic
...but the result is:
NULL

as.vector(stat[,1]) didn't work either.

Finally I just took a chance and tried:
as.vector(c(t20$statistic))
which gives me the statistic without the t. Don't ask me why...

Now I wonder if this is THE way to extract things from a output list 
where components have (or have not) attributes. Or if someone could 
briefly describe a more general case of how to extract numbers from 
several summaries (be it t.tests or not).

Thanks a lot for your help!

Sincerely,

Henrik  

