Not with lda (deliberately) and not AFAIK with discrim.

> The question one could raise is: why not simply using all the variables
> and stick to lda(...) instead of trying to complicate my life? If one
> has a good argument for doing so (that means not trying to select
> variables), I sure would be ready to forget my query about how to mimic
> SAS in S+.

That procedure is extremely sensitive to the assumptions of joint 
normality and common covariance.  Please use stepwise logistic 
discrimination instead -- it is a lot more robust.

