From timh at insightful.com  Tue Jan 11 20:50:08 2005
From: timh at insightful.com (Tim Hesterberg)
Date: Tue, 11 Jan 2005 12:50:08 -0800
Subject: Re: abline constraint
In-Reply-To: <001301c4f662$e45eea30$9100a8c0@awesomeness>
References: <001301c4f662$e45eea30$9100a8c0@awesomeness>
Message-ID: <SE2KEXCH01DN7BhBfFj00002ef6@se2kexch01.insightful.com>

>I am using the abline function to plot several regression lines on a plot.
>(e.g. abline(a.model)) It's quick and easy, but produces a line extending to
>the edges of the plot.
>
>Is it possible to constrain the abline to the data range of each regression?
>
>Regards,
>
>Brent
>
>D. Brenton Myers
>Research Specialist
>University of Missouri / USDA-ARS-Croping Systems and Water Quality Unit

Use lines() or segments()

Here's a function I used for horizontal or vertical lines with
limited extent.  You could use the same idea for other cases.

abline2 _ function(h, v, xlim, ylim, ...){
  # Like abline, but using segments rather than lines, with
  # horizontal extent limited by xlim, vertical extent by ylim
  if(!missing(h)) segments( xlim[1], h, xlim[2], h, ...)
  if(!missing(v)) segments( v, ylim[1], v, ylim[2], ...)
}

