Yingmei,

That always happens to me too.  Its because the keys show up in both
datasets.  Depending on what join conditions you want, you may be able
to achieve some success with all.x=TRUE or FALSE and all.y=TRUE or
FALSE.

I use the following command to get rid of the duplicates, where out is
my matrix name and gvkey is what I am matching by:

out <- out[!duplicated(out$gvkey),]

HTH,

Roger

